```c
ocfs2_dlm_shutdown();
ocfs2_cluster_disconnect(osb->cconn, hangup_pending);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs when `ocfs2_mount_volume()` fails after the initialization of the DLM resources, leading to a call to `ocfs2_dlm_shutdown()` without any initialized resources. The unconditional call to `ocfs2_cluster_disconnect(osb->cconn, hangup_pending)` attempts to clean up the DLM connection (`osb->cconn`), which may be uninitialized, resulting in a kernel crash.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (osb->cconn) {
    ocfs2_cluster_disconnect(osb->cconn, hangup_pending);
    osb->cconn = NULL;
}
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a check to ensure that `osb->cconn` is valid before attempting to disconnect it. This prevents the function from trying to clean up an uninitialized resource, thereby avoiding the kernel crash that occurs when `ocfs2_dlm_shutdown()` is called without valid DLM resources.

